# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# What is NOT here
#
# Third-party material, vendor blobs, reverse-engineering scratch and the
# local documentation all live in ../hema-local, outside this tree entirely.
# See ../hema-local/README.md.
#
# That is deliberate. This file used to name each of them, which meant every
# new download or note needed a line adding, and anything that arrived without
# one got committed - which is how an x86-64 test binary ended up tracked.
# Keeping the material outside the repo means there is nothing to remember.
#
# So what remains below is only what is *generated in place* and therefore
# cannot live anywhere else, plus a short safety net for the few third-party
# things large enough that re-downloading one into this directory by accident
# would be worth catching.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# ---- generated in place ---------------------------------------------------

# Compiler and linker output.
*.o
*.d
*.elf
*.hex
*.map
*.lst
DA14585/
DA14531/
Debug/
Release/

# Host test binaries. Whitelisted by source type rather than named one by one,
# so a test added later is ignored without this file being touched.
firmware/hema_epd_clock/test/*
!firmware/hema_epd_clock/test/*.c
!firmware/hema_epd_clock/test/*.h
!firmware/hema_epd_clock/test/Makefile
!firmware/hema_epd_clock/test/stub/

# Self-signed TLS certificate and key made by webui/serve.py. Local to one
# machine and one LAN address, so there is nothing to share.
webui/.certs/

# Python and Node local state.
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.venv/
node_modules/

# Eclipse / e2 studio local state. The tracked .project/.cproject are generated
# by tools/gen_e2studio_project.py and are intentionally kept.
.metadata/
.settings/
*.launch

# ---- safety net -----------------------------------------------------------
# None of these belongs in the repo; all of them have a home in ../hema-local.
# Listed anyway because they are big, non-redistributable, or both, and an
# accidental `git add -A` after a download is easy to do and awkward to undo.

SDK_*/
SDK_*.zip
DA145xx_SDK/
e2studio_installer*.run
*.bin
*.img
